  "description": "PIWJEM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C54 H87 N10 O19 Sm3,C54 H91 N8 O15 Sm3 2+,4.8(C1 H4 O1),2(N1 O3 1-). From the CIF bond table, Sm3 (Sm) has 6 O neighbors; Sm4 (Sm) has 6 O neighbors; Sm3A (Sm) has 6 O neighbors; Sm1 (Sm) has 6 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 6 O neighbors; Sm1A (Sm) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.582-3.605 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.96-97.45°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C57H101N10O29Sm3. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
